From: SqueezeFS-Zig <sqz@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sqz: shmem: honour IOCB_NOWAIT in shmem_file_read_iter and set FMODE_NOWAIT, so an io_uring read of a resident memfd page completes inline instead of punting to io-wq

PROPOSED (scripts/kernel/proposed/, not in the series): compile-checked
as mm/shmem.o against the 7.2.8 omarchy-sqz tree with 0001-0030 applied;
NOT booted, NOT measured. The owner builds and boots; the daemon-side
probe plan is below.

Why (docs/evidence/rung-10-read-view.md). Under zero copy every byte the
daemon produces in RAM reaches the app's pages by one io_uring
READ_FIXED(memfd -> zc slot): the bounce window of a served reply, the
fill-pool slab of a warm serve (SQUEEZEFS_READ_ZC_SERVE), an inline or
staged file's body. shmem files carry no FMODE_NOWAIT (shmem_file_open
sets FMODE_CAN_ODIRECT alone) and are not pollable, so
io_file_supports_nowait() answers false and io_read() returns -EAGAIN at
issue for EVERY such read: io_uring punts it to an io-wq worker, which
then performs a plain blocking read of a page that was resident all
along. Measured on the FUSE boundary ruler (rung-10-fuse-boundary.md):
the `bounce` arm costs 2.6 cores of io-wq at 2.1 M reads/s beside the
7.7 cores of the workers — 1.2 us of CPU and one wake-and-switch per
served 4 KiB, for a 4 KiB copy that is 0.1 us.

What: shmem_file_read_iter() takes a non-blocking path under
IOCB_NOWAIT — a resident, up-to-date folio is served (unlocked, as the
SGP_READ path serves it: it unlocks before the copy), a hole its zeros,
and anything that would wait (a swapped-out entry, a folio not up to date
or being truncated) is -EAGAIN, which io_uring answers by its ordinary
punt — and shmem_file_open() declares FMODE_NOWAIT so the ring issues
reads non-blocking in the first place. Writes are unchanged (no
FMODE_NOWAIT write path is claimed: shmem_file_write_iter() takes the
inode lock and may allocate; io_uring keeps punting them, as today).

Probe plan: the boundary ruler's `bounce` arm before and after the boot
(io-wq cores per read at equal IOPS; `iou-wrk-*` threads absent from
the daemon's class table), then the warm 4k randread rows (a working
set inside the hot tier, SQUEEZEFS_READ_ZC_SERVE on), THE KILL MATRIX
and the zc e2e rows.
---
 mm/shmem.c | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/mm/shmem.c
+++ b/mm/shmem.c
@@ -2917,7 +2917,12 @@
 
 static int shmem_file_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
 {
-	file->f_mode |= FMODE_CAN_ODIRECT;
+	/*
+	 * FMODE_NOWAIT: shmem_file_read_iter() honours IOCB_NOWAIT, so an
+	 * io_uring read of a resident page completes inline instead of
+	 * being punted to io-wq for want of the flag.
+	 */
+	file->f_mode |= FMODE_CAN_ODIRECT | FMODE_NOWAIT;
 	return generic_file_open(inode, file);
 }
 
@@ -3307,15 +3312,40 @@
 			break;
 
 		index = iocb->ki_pos >> PAGE_SHIFT;
-		error = shmem_get_folio(inode, index, 0, &folio, SGP_READ);
-		if (error) {
-			if (error == -EINVAL)
-				error = 0;
-			break;
+		if (iocb->ki_flags & IOCB_NOWAIT) {
+			/*
+			 * Non-blocking: serve a resident, up-to-date folio
+			 * (unlocked: the copy below needs no lock, as the
+			 * SGP_READ path unlocks before it copies) or a hole's
+			 * zeros; anything that would wait — a swapped-out
+			 * page, a folio under I/O or being truncated — is
+			 * -EAGAIN, and the caller retries from a context that
+			 * may block.
+			 */
+			folio = filemap_get_entry(mapping, index);
+			if (xa_is_value(folio)) {
+				folio = NULL;
+				error = -EAGAIN;
+				break;
+			}
+			if (folio && (!folio_test_uptodate(folio) ||
+				      folio->mapping != mapping)) {
+				folio_put(folio);
+				error = -EAGAIN;
+				break;
+			}
+		} else {
+			error = shmem_get_folio(inode, index, 0, &folio,
+						SGP_READ);
+			if (error) {
+				if (error == -EINVAL)
+					error = 0;
+				break;
+			}
+			if (folio)
+				folio_unlock(folio);
 		}
 		if (folio) {
-			folio_unlock(folio);
-
 			page = folio_file_page(folio, index);
 			if (PageHWPoison(page)) {
 				folio_put(folio);
